# Everything ships from the working tree: npm packs the files as they are on
# disk, so a checkout with core.autocrlf=true published 0.12.1 with CRLF in 45
# of its 105 files (SKILL.md, the .svelte components, base.css, LICENSE), and a
# consumer comparing the skill byte for byte on Linux went red. LF in every
# text file, on every checkout; the generator of src/tokens.css writes LF too.
# CRLF only for the Windows scripts that need it. After changing these lines:
#   git add --renormalize .
* text=auto eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
